WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.087
Gate 8 begins by writing each
wave as an attribute query.

2
00:00:04.087 --> 00:00:08.347
Because waves are defined by
attribute values rather than OUs,

3
00:00:08.347 --> 00:00:12.688
each wave's scope is a query, and
its dynamic groups already exist.

4
00:00:12.688 --> 00:00:16.757
Each track picks members from its
own source: users by HR codes,

5
00:00:16.757 --> 00:00:21.943
devices by what provisioning writes on
them, servers by resource group and tag,

6
00:00:21.943 --> 00:00:25.613
and non-person identities by
their owning application.

7
00:00:25.613 --> 00:00:28.787
Start with the lowest-risk
region and a pilot division,

8
00:00:28.787 --> 00:00:32.807
then two or three divisions at a time,
each drift-clean before the next,

9
00:00:32.807 --> 00:00:36.051
with drift detection running
daily from the first wave.

10
00:00:36.051 --> 00:00:40.813
GPO links come off a migrated
OU only after seven clean days.

11
00:00:40.813 --> 00:00:44.512
The rule shown is the kit's
fixture form, with its guards.

12
00:00:44.512 --> 00:00:47.611
And in every wave, leaver
automation goes first,

13
00:00:47.611 --> 00:00:51.480
because revocation is where
the risk and the evidence are.
